# CSS codes, the Calderbank-Shor-Steane construction that turns a pair of nested classical codes into a quantum code. A
# quantum code must protect against two kinds of error at once, bit flips and phase flips, and the CSS trick handles them
# separately: one classical code guards the bit-flip, X-type, errors, and its dual guards the phase-flip, Z-type, errors.
# The two error kinds are exchanged by the Hadamard transform, which swaps X and Z, so the X-sector and Z-sector of a CSS
# code are dual halves of one structure. This file MODELS the two error sectors and DEFINES the Hadamard duality that
# swaps them, then PROVES it is an involution, swapping twice returns each sector, so the two halves are symmetric. The
# Steane code's logical dimension and the perfect five-qubit code's saturation of the quantum Hamming bound are recorded
# as machine-integer facts. The duality involution is proved over the actual sector type by induction.

# The two error sectors of a CSS code: the bit-flip X-type and the phase-flip Z-type.
form sector
  case x-type
  case z-type

# The Hadamard duality swaps the two sectors, exchanging bit-flip and phase-flip errors.
task hadamard
  take s, like sector
  like sector
  fork case, read s
    case x-type
      send back
        make z-type
    case z-type
      send back
        make x-type

# THE HADAMARD DUALITY IS AN INVOLUTION: applying it twice returns each sector, hadamard (hadamard s) = s, for every
# sector, so the X and Z halves of a CSS code are symmetric duals. Proved by induction over the two sectors.
rule hadamard-duality-is-an-involution
  seat s, like sector
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call hadamard
        call hadamard
          read s
      read s
  fold s

# THE HADAMARD SWAPS THE SECTORS: it sends the X-type sector to the Z-type, hadamard x-type = z-type, exchanging bit-flip
# for phase-flip, so a self-dual code protects against both equally.
rule the-hadamard-swaps-the-sectors
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call hadamard
        make x-type
      make z-type
  calm hold

# THE STEANE CODE encodes one logical qubit, as a machine-integer fact: built from the [7,4,3] Hamming code of dimension
# four and its dual of dimension three, the CSS logical count is the difference, 4 - 3 = 1.
hold steane-encodes-one-logical-qubit
  call is-equal
    code 1
    call subtract
      code 4
      code 3

# THE FIVE-QUBIT CODE is perfect, saturating the quantum Hamming bound: 2^(5-1) = 16 syndromes exactly equal the one
# identity plus three Pauli errors on each of five qubits, 1 + 3 * 5 = 16, no syndrome wasted.
hold five-qubit-code-is-perfect
  call is-equal
    code 16
    call add
      code 1
      call multiply
        code 3
        code 5
